1
00:00:00,029 --> 00:00:04,250
In Omni Dispatch, open New Call
for a community outreach standby.

2
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:08,560
Enter a name your team will
recognize and use Nature to describe

3
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:09,899
what responders need to know.

4
00:00:10,340 --> 00:00:12,829
This exercise uses Medical and Routine.

5
00:00:13,279 --> 00:00:16,620
Choose the type and priority your
department uses for this work.

6
00:00:16,759 --> 00:00:21,870
On the location section, select GPS
and enter the latitude and longitude.

7
00:00:22,359 --> 00:00:24,430
Check the map against your intended site.

8
00:00:24,869 --> 00:00:28,299
A search team can use coordinates
for a trail rendezvous, and an

9
00:00:28,299 --> 00:00:31,390
industrial response team can
use them for an access gate.

10
00:00:31,520 --> 00:00:35,750
Use the contact picker if an existing
department contact belongs on the call.

11
00:00:36,139 --> 00:00:38,949
Here we select Academy Community Partners.

12
00:00:39,369 --> 00:00:42,759
Check Save as pending and
select Save Pending Call.

13
00:00:43,139 --> 00:00:46,929
The call now has a number in Pending
Calls, where dispatch can find it

14
00:00:46,929 --> 00:00:48,780
again when it is ready for release.

15
00:00:48,919 --> 00:00:51,290
Open the pending call and start dispatch.

16
00:00:51,659 --> 00:00:54,820
In the recipient picker,
select the intended recipient.

17
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:56,989
Here we choose Wallace Boden.

18
00:00:57,359 --> 00:01:00,190
Check the selection count
on Done before confirming.

19
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:03,449
Back in the console, find
the same call number under

20
00:01:03,449 --> 00:01:05,679
Active Calls and open Details.

21
00:01:05,879 --> 00:01:10,120
Select Notes and enter an update that
will make sense to the next dispatcher.

22
00:01:10,510 --> 00:01:13,780
Save it, then verify that the
entry appears on the call.

23
00:01:14,249 --> 00:01:18,220
A security desk could record when
site staff completed a handoff, and

24
00:01:18,220 --> 00:01:21,899
a wildland contractor could record
where the relief crew should report.

25
00:01:22,029 --> 00:01:26,150
Use Call actions and Edit Call to
update the incident description.

26
00:01:26,599 --> 00:01:28,780
Verify the revised wording on the call.

27
00:01:29,210 --> 00:01:32,949
When the exercise is over,
choose Close Call, confirm the

28
00:01:32,949 --> 00:01:34,960
reason and enter a closeout note.

29
00:01:35,359 --> 00:01:38,760
Review Notify everyone who was
dispatched before confirming.

30
00:01:39,110 --> 00:01:41,430
In this training exercise we leave it off.

31
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:44,750
Back in the console, search
for the call and verify that

32
00:01:44,750 --> 00:01:46,300
it has left the active queue.

33
00:01:46,809 --> 00:01:50,530
In this exercise we can also
open History on a nearby call.

34
00:01:50,999 --> 00:01:54,499
Match the original call number
and read its Closed status under

35
00:01:54,499 --> 00:01:56,490
Previous calls at this location.

